/-!
# Triality: the upper half of E.1.14(2)

For every normal copy L of the genuine graph-field group ³D₄(2^f), f>0,
in a finite group G=LT, `isEGenerated_of_triality` proves E-generation
with bound 3f. `not_odd_card_of_triality` proves even order. The calculation
uses the actual residual local factors with PSL₂(2^(3f)) and PSL₂(2^f)
quotients, including the solvable central-node exception at f=1.

The conjugation-invariant elementary family and proper-subgroup obstruction
at 3f-1 are still required for equality. No lower bound is asserted here.
The parent `ValuesEvenExceptional` owns the minimum/final assembly.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith E.1.14(2), printed p.214 (`refs/quasithin.pdf`).
-/
